                <head>209. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 9, the Department of the Navy directed United States Naval forces in the
                    Eastern Atlantic and Mediteranean that no United States Navy or military supply
                    ships would transit the Suez Canal (scheduled to reopen on March 15) until an
                    agreement was reached, satisfactory to the United States Government, regarding
                    tolls and other interim arrangements for the operation of the Canal. These
                    orders were transmitted to CINCNELM in telegram 20522, March 9. (Department of
                    State, NEA/IAI Files: Lot 69 D 488, Suez Canal Settlement 1957)</p>
            </div>
